{
  "version": "0.5.5-beta.12",
  "notes": "## Changes since `v0.5.5-beta.11`\n\n### Features\n\n- switch to tabs 1-9 with Cmd+1-9 by default on macOS, since Terminal, iTerm2 and browsers use it there while Option+digit types symbols and is a readline count once Option acts as Meta; Windows and Linux keep Alt+1-9, and saved custom bindings are untouched ([d8ea9ad8](https://github.com/330079598/tTerm/commit/d8ea9ad8855207a1fa99fb5a150910606b7dd3b7))\n\n### Fixes\n\n- switch to the Nth tab from the chord's digit instead of event.key, since Option+1 on macOS types \"¡\", so the shortcut matched by physical key but the handler read no digit and the tab never changed ([c6219b5f](https://github.com/330079598/tTerm/commit/c6219b5f1d36e0966f567c3eb80a28718e8b41e0))\n\n### Other changes\n\n- expect dead_code on NotificationPermission::TaskbarBadgesOff on macOS, since only Windows reports it and the enum's allow covers every other platform, so clippy failed on macOS ([9606f952](https://github.com/330079598/tTerm/commit/9606f952f75a3a9dd924788724605cbed58e7b5c))\n- walk the tray icon's pixels with as_chunks_mut instead of chunks_exact_mut, since clippy 1.99's chunks_exact_to_as_chunks lint failed CI on the constant chunk size ([91a26ea6](https://github.com/330079598/tTerm/commit/91a26ea6ffff2ac5c99cbb50ab3c251373e607bb))\n\n**Full comparison:** [v0.5.5-beta.11...v0.5.5-beta.12](https://github.com/330079598/tTerm/compare/v0.5.5-beta.11...v0.5.5-beta.12)",
